title: "BlasCh: BLAST-based false positive chimera detection and recovery for metabarcoding and eDNA datasets"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-05-07
url: "https://github.com/alihkz94/BlasCh"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/alihkz94/BlasCh"
abstract: >-
  BlasCh is a command-line tool that identifies and recovers false positive
  chimeric sequences from metabarcoding and environmental DNA (eDNA) datasets.
  It builds per-sample BLAST self-databases and optionally searches a reference
  database to classify sequences as non-chimeric, borderline, or true chimeras
  based on user-configurable identity and coverage thresholds.
keywords:
  - metabarcoding
  - eDNA
  - chimera detection
  - chimera recovery
  - BLAST
  - bioinformatics
  - amplicon sequencing
